+// The rim is lit from a height field, after liquid-glass (ryohsuke1231, MIT): the edge of the
+// glass is a superellipse slope whose normal catches a light from fresnel_angle; the inner
+// shadow is the ambient-occlusion band inside that edge. Both act within the refraction band,
+// so the flat interior keeps its fast path. All widths are fractions of the band.
